{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he shall fill his palms</b> — two instances; one is this, and the other: \"and he shall fill the rope\" (to restore life), in connection with Joab — for by merit of the Yom Kippur service they were victorious in war." "<b>Fine spices</b> — in gematria: <b>דקה</b> (fine) = <b>מדקה</b> (from crushing)." "<b>Fine</b> — two instances; one is this, and the other: \"and after the fire, a sound of thin silence\" (דקה) — this is \"for in a cloud I will appear upon the cover.\" That is: in the cloud of the incense, concerning which <b>דקה</b> is stated, there will be \"a sound of thin silence\" (דקה), and the glory of YHWH will appear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:37.451561933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}